    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1631">

                <pb facs="1184" n="1068" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1068"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/139.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 31, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Referring to previous
                    correspondence in regard to Mr. Henri Huguet, a French citizen, who was recently
                    arrested at Santa Engracia, Mexico, I am pleased to inform you that the
                    Department is in receipt of a telegram from the American Consulate General at
                    Monterey, Mexico, dated August 28, stating that Mr. Huguet has telegraphed the
                    Consulate General, announcing his safe arrival at his home.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
